    rationale:
      "Dispatched a research agent (read-only) to run the standard five tiers (Convex/SQLite parity, security/injection, untested orchestration, money/ledger integrity, docs staleness) scoped specifically at the files changed in that diff window, after reading every one of them in full. It found a genuine docs-staleness gap (tier 5): src/app/docs/architecture/page.tsx's Phase-5/bundle-fulfillment narrative (the paragraph immediately following the original resendBundleBuyerEmailAction writeup) still described that action's old, now fully-replaced detect-after-send design as current -- claiming it re-reads the handoff immediately before persisting each marker and, if the fresh read already shows a marker this call itself just sent, skips writing a duplicate note and reports success: false with an explicit duplicate-notification warning. The bundle-buyer-email-resend-race-guard-ordering-fix entry (same diff window, PR #897) replaced that entire mechanism with reserve-then-send-then-release (reserveBundleBuyerEmailNotes/releaseBundleBuyerEmailNotes) specifically because the old design could only detect a lost race after the real duplicate email had already gone out, not prevent it -- and a new, accurate paragraph describing the fix was correctly appended later in the same file. But the earlier, more prominent in-narrative paragraph was never updated or removed, leaving two contradictory descriptions of the same function in one document: a reader relying on the earlier section (embedded in the bundle-fulfillment walkthrough, rather than the later append-only fix log) would come away believing a real duplicate-email race still exists today, when it was closed in the very same PR that added the later paragraph. Independently re-verified by reading both paragraphs directly (page.tsx lines ~1536-1552 and ~4328-4359 before the fix) and confirming resendBundleBuyerEmailAction's actual current source no longer contains any post-send re-read/detect logic at all -- the reserve happens before either send, matching only the later paragraph.\n\nThe research agent otherwise reported the diff clean across all five tiers: the reserve/release race guard is atomic on both Convex (single mutation, re-check-then-patch) and SQLite (synchronous read-then-write, no await between); both new Convex mutations are registered on the static API map in db.ts in the same commit as the table logic; captureError's webhook URL is http(s)-validated, the secret goes in an Authorization header never the URL, every payload field (message/stack/context) is length-capped, and the call is best-effort/non-throwing/timeout-bounded; the webhook's new outer try/catch correctly wraps the entire switch and re-throws unchanged, preserving every case's existing early 5xx returns and Stripe's retry contract; every new function (captureError, buildErrorTrackingPayload, the reserve/release mutations and SQLite twins, the rewritten dashboard action) has dedicated Vitest coverage.\n\nFixed by rewriting the stale paragraph (page.tsx lines 1536-1552) to describe the current reserve-then-send-then-release design in the same amount of detail the surrounding narrative uses, and pointing the reader to the fuller mechanism writeup further down the same document rather than duplicating it verbatim. Pure documentation fix -- no source/logic/test change, since the underlying race guard itself was already correct and already covered; only the prose describing it was wrong. No new Vitest cases needed (nothing executable changed); ran the full existing suite to confirm zero regression.\n\nsrc/lib/process/business-decisions.ts -- this entry. src/lib/process/prompt_process.tsx -- the accompanying ITERATIONS entry. No NEXT_STEPS change -- all five gated items (stripe-price-objects, lead-ingestion, marketing-content-scheduling, commerce-payouts-stripe-connect, github-actions-runner-unavailable) remain operator/legal/infra-blocked, unchanged. Diff-gate anchor moves to 20d1184f (this session's own starting tip, post-PR-#900).\n\nFile-size check per AGENT_PROTOCOL's re-archive note: prompt_process.tsx 237,031 bytes, business-decisions.ts 220,025 bytes at session start (both via wc -c) -- both comfortably under the 262,144-byte trigger, no re-archive needed this round.\n\nVerified: npm ci (413 packages, matching the documented baseline) + npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json (0 errors) + npm run lint (clean) + npx vitest run full suite (3596 passed, 211 files -- unchanged, no new tests since this is docs-only) + a full clean rebuild (rm -rf .next && npm run build, clean, same route split, no new warnings) + npm run dev smoke check curling /docs/architecture (200; confirmed via grep that the stale duplicate-notification phrase is gone and the new paragraph's reserveBundleBuyerEmailNotes reference renders), /dashboard/leads (200), and /preview/example-bakery (200). Killed the dev server, removed the stray gitignored local.db/local.db-shm/local.db-wal it created, and confirmed git status showed only the intended three process-log/docs files changed before this commit.",
