    rationale:
      "A dispatched research agent, told the observability/captureError axis was now fully closed (webhook writes, checkout session creation, all db.ts read paths, Resend sends) and not to propose wiring another site, found a genuine residual gap in a DIFFERENT already-shipped fix from earlier today: buffer-schedule-stale-pack-content-guard added a marketing-pack freshness re-check inside scheduleMarketingPackToBufferAction's outer for-loop, once per Buffer profile, to stop a concurrent generateMarketingPackAction regenerate from letting the loop post now-superseded copy. But that fix only re-checked once per profile, not once per Buffer post - and the code's own inner loop (queuing every matching variant for a content type, not just the first, since MONTHLY_MARKETING_PACK_TYPES generates 3 facebook_caption/instagram_caption variants per lead per month) makes several sequential awaited createBufferUpdate calls per profile when a profile matches more than one variant. A regenerate landing between the first and second variant post for the SAME profile still shipped the superseded copy on that profile's remaining posts, since the one freshness check for that profile had already passed before the first variant posted. This is the exact same 'already-shipped superseded copy to a live, unrecallable social-media post' failure the original fix targeted, just with a narrower but still-real window (within one profile's own posting pass, not only between different profiles) - confirmed directly by reading the code (src/app/dashboard/leads/actions.ts, scheduleMarketingPackToBufferAction) and buffer-actions.test.ts's existing two regenerate-detection tests, both of which only exercise the between-profile boundary with single-variant-per-profile fixtures.\n\nFixed by moving the freshness re-check (getMarketingPack + generatedAt comparison) out of the per-profile position and into the innermost per-variant loop, immediately before each createBufferUpdate call, rather than once per profileId. On detecting staleness mid-profile, breaks out of the inner loop (stopping the remaining variants for that profile) rather than continuing to the next profile directly - the outer loop's next profileId iteration naturally re-checks freshness itself and will also detect the same staleness, cascading the skip to every remaining profile exactly as before, so no explicit early-exit-the-whole-function logic was needed. The skip message now uses the same label variable already computed for scheduled/failed entries (profileId alone when a profile matches only one variant, profileId (N/total) when it matches more than one), so the existing single-variant tests' skip-message assertions are unaffected - the label format only changes observably for the newly-covered multi-variant-per-profile case.\n\nShipped: src/app/dashboard/leads/actions.ts - restructured scheduleMarketingPackToBufferAction so the profile/contentType/variants-existence checks run first (unchanged), then the freshness re-check moved inside the per-variant for-loop directly before its createBufferUpdate call, replacing the removed per-profile-level check. src/app/dashboard/leads/buffer-actions.test.ts - added one new test (a single profile with 3 matching variants, a regenerate landing between the first and second createBufferUpdate call, asserting only the first variant posts and the remaining two are skipped with the per-variant label). Verified the new test actually catches the regression: git stash'd actions.ts's source change alone (test file kept) and confirmed the new assertion failed (all 3 variants posted instead of 1) before restoring the fix; all 35 pre-existing buffer-actions.test.ts cases (including both existing regenerate-detection tests) still pass unchanged, confirming the refactor is behavior-preserving for the cases it already covered. Added one paragraph to /docs/architecture directly after checkout-session-record-capture-error-wiring's writeup. src/lib/process/business-decisions.ts - this entry. src/lib/process/prompt_process.tsx - a new NEXT_STEPS done entry plus this ITERATIONS entry. No NEXT_STEPS change - the five gated items (stripe-price-objects, lead-ingestion, marketing-content-scheduling, commerce-payouts-stripe-connect, github-actions-runner-unavailable) remain operator/legal/infra-blocked. Diff-gate anchor moves to 73bd1328 (origin/main tip after PR #908 merged, this session's own starting point for this iteration).\n\nFile-size check per AGENT_PROTOCOL's re-archive note: both prompt_process.tsx (198,849 bytes) and business-decisions.ts (122,523 bytes) measured well under the 262,144-byte trigger before this entry, thanks to PR #907's re-archive split earlier today - no re-archive needed this round.\n\nVerified: npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json (0 errors) + npm run lint (clean) + npx vitest run targeted (buffer-actions.test.ts, 36/36 passed) then full suite (3607 passed, 212 files - 1 net new) + a full clean rebuild (rm -rf .next && npm run build, clean, same route split, no new warnings). No dev-server smoke check needed beyond the automated build/test/lint gate - server-action-only change with no new route/UI surface, gated behind ALLOW_MARKETING_SCHEDULING and requiring a live Buffer token neither available in this sandboxed environment.",
